<p class="lead">If you are planning a new website, the first question is usually about cost. The second question is almost always about time. How long does it take to build a website? The honest answer: anywhere from a few hours to over a year. The real answer depends on what you are building, how you are building it, and how prepared you are when the project starts.</p>

        <p>This guide breaks down realistic timelines for every type of website build in 2026. We cover DIY builders, template-based sites, custom agency builds, and enterprise platforms. We also walk through each phase of the process, identify the most common causes of delay, and show you how to keep your project on schedule.</p>

        <h2>Timeline by Build Method: The Honest Breakdown</h2>
        <p>The method you choose to build your website is the single biggest factor in how long it takes. Each approach has a different timeline, trade-off, and outcome. Here is what you can realistically expect.</p>

        <div class="timeline-table">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Build Method</th>
                <th>Timeline</th>
                <th>Best For</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>DIY Website Builder</strong><br><small>(Wix, Squarespace, Namecheap)</small></td>
                <td>1–3 days</td>
                <td>Hobby projects, personal sites, testing ideas</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Template + Freelancer</strong></td>
